# Docker build context excludes (#625). Every entry says why it is excluded.
# Only exclude what the image never needs; anything an operator might want to
# bake in (Dockerfile, compose file, monitoring configs) stays in the context.

# --- Python build/cache artefacts: regenerated inside the image ---------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# --- Local virtualenvs: the image installs requirements.txt itself ------------
env/
venv/
ENV/
.venv/

# --- Test/coverage output: never shipped ---------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.cover
.hypothesis/

# --- Docs: not needed at runtime (README kept for the package metadata) --------
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Editor files ----------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- VCS metadata: large and irrelevant to the build ----------------------------
.git/
.gitignore

# --- Runtime data and logs: mounted as volumes (./data, ./logs), never baked ---
data/
logs/
*.log

# --- Rust build output: kafka-delta-ingest is compiled from source, and a
#     local target/ dir is multiple GB -------------------------------------------
kafka-delta-ingest/target/

# --- CI config: not used inside containers ----------------------------------------
.github/

# Monitoring: configs/dashboards stay out of the image; the exporter code ships
# for the `metrics` Dockerfile target (#449).
monitoring/*
!monitoring/__init__.py
!monitoring/metrics_exporter.py
!monitoring/metric_helpers.py

# --- Kubernetes manifests/Helm chart: applied with kubectl/helm from the repo,
#     never read inside a container --------------------------------------------------
k8s/

# Deliberately NOT excluded:
# - Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, .dockerignore: small, and tools such as
#   BuildKit frontends / compose-in-image / SBOM scanners expect them.
# - monitoring exporter modules (metrics_exporter.py, metric_helpers.py): the
#   `metrics` target runs them (#449). The configs are excluded above because
#   docker-compose bind-mounts monitoring/prometheus.yml and monitoring/alerting
#   at runtime, so edits apply without a rebuild.
